-- title:
--   An admissible control process of the trade execution problem
-- statement:
--   **An admissible control process of the trade execution problem** (Bäuerle & Rieder, *Markov Decision Processes with Applications to Finance* (2011), §9.4, pp.293–294, PDF 303–304): an $(F_t)$-predictable process $\pi _t \in  \mathbb N _0$ (the number of shares the agent would like to sell at $t$, executed only if $t$ is a jump time of the Poisson process) with $\pi _t \le  X_t$.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $F_t$ is generated by the Poisson process, so a predictable process is $\pi _t = g_n(t - T_n; S_0, \dots , S_{n-1}; T_n, Z_n)$ for $t \in  (T_n, T_{n+1}]$ with measurable $g_n$ (Remark 8.1.2; $S_j$ the sojourn times, $Z_n = X_{T_n}$). Admissibility $\pi _t \le  X_t = Z_n$ on $(T_n, T_{n+1}]$ is required of $g_n$ at every argument, which loses no cost: the values off the reachable arguments are never used and can be set to $0$.
-- source:
--   Bäuerle & Rieder, Markov Decision Processes with Applications to Finance (2011), §9.4, pp.293–294, PDF 303–304

import Mathlib

namespace BauerleRiederMDP.LQ.Supplement

/-- **An admissible control process of the trade execution problem** (Bäuerle & Rieder, *Markov
Decision Processes with Applications to Finance* (2011), §9.4, pp.293–294, PDF 303–304): an
`(F_t)`-predictable process `π_t ∈ ℕ_0` (the number of shares the agent would like to sell at `t`,
executed only if `t` is a jump time of the Poisson process) with `π_t ≤ X_t`.

**Formalization Note.** `F_t` is generated by the Poisson process, so a predictable process is
`π_t = g_n(t − T_n; S_0, …, S_{n−1}; T_n, Z_n)` for `t ∈ (T_n, T_{n+1}]` with measurable `g_n`
(Remark 8.1.2; `S_j` the sojourn times, `Z_n = X_{T_n}`). Admissibility `π_t ≤ X_t = Z_n` on
`(T_n, T_{n+1}]` is required of `g_n` at every argument, which loses no cost: the values off the
reachable arguments are never used and can be set to `0`. -/
def TradeStrategy : Type :=
  (n : ℕ) → {g : ℝ × ((Fin n → ℝ) × (ℝ × ℕ)) → ℕ // Measurable g ∧ ∀ q, g q ≤ q.2.2.2}

end BauerleRiederMDP.LQ.Supplement


